# Trivy ignore file — the "CVE with no fix yet" policy in practice.
#
# Rule: we HARD-BLOCK on CRITICAL/HIGH that have a fixed version (ignore-unfixed:true
# already drops unfixed ones from the gate). When we must accept a fixable finding
# temporarily, it goes here WITH a justification and an expiry date, and is tracked
# as a ticket. An empty/rationale-only file means "nothing is being suppressed."
#
# Format: <CVE-ID> then a comment. Example of how an accepted-with-expiry entry looks:
#
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # accepted 2026-07-29, expires 2026-08-29: no fixed release upstream,
#                 # not reachable from our code path (transitive, dev-only). Ticket SEC-123.
#
# Currently: no suppressions. The hardened image upgrades every starter dependency to a
# patched release, so the gate is expected to pass with zero exceptions.
